+// Mirror pacing: Telegram throttles bursts to one chat. A 429 means the message
+// was NOT accepted, so waiting retry_after and sending again cannot duplicate.
+// A network error raised before a connection to Telegram exists means the request never
+// left this machine, so the record was certainly not delivered and a retry cannot
+// duplicate it. Anything else (reset, socket error, timeout after connect) stays ambiguous.
+const NOT_SENT_CODES = new Set([
